# Copy to .env and adjust. Never commit .env.
KASHROOT_ENV=local

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Local stack (`docker compose up`) — Postgres+PostGIS on 5433, Redis, MinIO.
# This is the default: with no Supabase variables set, the app runs entirely
# against the containers and needs nothing else.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
KASHROOT_DATABASE_URL=postgresql+psycopg://kashroot:kashroot@localhost:5433/kashroot
KASHROOT_REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379/0

# Evidence photos (S3-compatible). Local dev points at MinIO.
KASHROOT_S3_ENDPOINT_URL=http://localhost:9000
KASHROOT_S3_BUCKET=kashroot-evidence
KASHROOT_S3_ACCESS_KEY=
KASHROOT_S3_SECRET_KEY=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Supabase — hosted Postgres + Storage. Setting the two SUPABASE_ variables below
# is all it takes: KASHROOT_STORAGE_BACKEND defaults to "auto", which switches
# evidence photos to Supabase Storage as soon as they are present, and back to
# MinIO/S3 when they are not.
#
# Supabase IS Postgres, so the models, the match engine and every Alembic
# migration are unchanged — only the URL moves.
#
# First-run checklist:
#   1. alembic upgrade head        (creates PostGIS + pg_trgm in `public`)
#   2. kashroot storage-check --create-bucket
#   3. kashroot db-check
# Do NOT also enable PostGIS from the Supabase dashboard: that installs it into
# the `extensions` schema, and you would then need KASHROOT_DB_SEARCH_PATH below.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Connection string: dashboard → Connect → TRANSACTION POOLER tab.
# Do NOT use the 'Direct connection' tab: db.<ref>.supabase.co is IPv6-only and
# fails DNS resolution on an IPv4-only machine. Pooler usernames carry the project
# ref (postgres.<ref>), direct ones do not.
# Swap the scheme to postgresql+psycopg:// — the bare postgresql:// resolves to
# psycopg2, which cannot take the pooler settings. Port 6543 is the running app;
# prepared statements are disabled automatically for it.
# KASHROOT_DATABASE_URL=postgresql+psycopg://postgres.<project-ref>:<db-password>@aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres
#
# Run `alembic upgrade head` against the SESSION POOLER tab (port 5432) instead —
# DDL wants one stable server session:
# KASHROOT_DATABASE_URL=postgresql+psycopg://postgres.<project-ref>:<db-password>@aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres

# Project URL: Project Settings → API.
# KEY: use the SECRET key (sb_secret_...) from Project Settings → API Keys →
# Secret keys — or the legacy service_role key on older projects. NOT the
# PUBLISHABLE key (sb_publishable_...) and NOT the legacy anon key: those are the
# client-side keys, bound by Row Level Security, and cannot create a bucket or
# write evidence photos. Startup rejects them with an explanation.
# The secret key bypasses Row Level Security. It is a SERVER-ONLY secret —
# never put it in the web app, a mobile client, or any client-side bundle.
# KASHROOT_SUPABASE_URL=https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
# KASHROOT_SUPABASE_SERVICE_KEY=
# KASHROOT_SUPABASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=kashroot-evidence

# Force a backend instead of auto-detecting: supabase | s3 | memory | auto
# KASHROOT_STORAGE_BACKEND=auto

# Only if PostGIS was enabled from the Supabase dashboard (extensions schema):
# KASHROOT_DB_SEARCH_PATH=public,extensions

# Override the automatic transaction-pooler detection. Leave unset.
# KASHROOT_DB_PREPARED_STATEMENTS=false

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Everything else
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Default certifier staleness window in days (see data/README.md).
KASHROOT_DEFAULT_FRESHNESS_DAYS=365
